Here's **NEAR-SIDE**, a fully autonomous cave-flying game. The ship runs a layered controller (strong short-range wall steering, mid-range centering toward the opening ahead, plus a soft attractor that pulls it back when drifting off course) while the cave ceiling and floor are shaped from scrolling multi-octave noise — with a difficulty ramp, near-miss sparks, a wipeout-and-refix loop, and a live telemetry HUD.

